File Index

/index.ts
Purpose: The only file main.tsx imports (dynamically, behind __SIMULACRUM_ADMIN_LOCAL__). It imports ./loader lazily inside the flag check; a static import of loader here would pull the marker into every build. Tests: index.test.ts (flag false never loads the loader; independent of the Copilot flag), main.simulacrumAdmin.test.tsx.

/loader.ts
Purpose: Builds the page's one runtime on first use and hands every caller the same object (startSimulacrumAdmin at page load and the window), and disposes it on `pagehide`. It wires the clearing: the connection runtime's onDeactivate clears the GMCP buffer and the character info, so nothing captured from the simulacrum outlives the connection. Later phases add their subscriptions and put each unsubscribe in dispose().

/connectionGate.ts
Purpose: The rules for "connected to the simulacrum": host AND port must both be accepted (defaults plus the owner's additions from localStorage `simulacrumAdmin.hosts`). A convenience gate, not a security boundary. The additions hold only what differs from the defaults (SETTINGS-01) and every reader goes through normalizeAdditions (E19). The owner's LAN address must never appear in this folder or its tests (LOCAL-05): tests build private-range values from parts. It deliberately does not import features/copilot/config.ts, whose address check it copies: the two features share nothing.

/runtime.ts
Purpose: Follows game:remote-server:open/close and exposes {connected, host, port, active} as an external store, plus onDeactivate callbacks that later phases use to clear buffers (E2). Its listeners use the keys simulacrumAdmin::connection-open/close on purpose: the shared dispatcher keeps ONE listener per key and the default key would replace the app's own (plan amendment A1, E26). Any new ListenEvent in this folder needs its own key too.

/marker.ts
Purpose: The string check:local-only searches a production dist for. scripts/check-local-only.mjs reads the constant from this file with a regex, so renaming SIMULACRUM_ADMIN_BUNDLE_MARKER or moving the file breaks the guard on purpose (a missing constant is an error, not a pass).

/tabs.ts
Purpose: The window six tabs in display order and their placeholder lines, kept out of the component so the component file only exports components (react-refresh). A later phase replaces a placeholder by mounting the tab component in SimulacrumAdminWindow.tsx; keep the order and ids stable, the panel ids derive from them.

/gmcpCapture.ts
Purpose: The GMCP buffer: newest 1000 messages, memory only, stored ONLY while the connection runtime says the socket is the simulacrum (the live DSL game never lands here), cleared when it leaves. Does NOT use features/gmcp/gmcpRouter.ts (that one drops unknown packages; this one must show exactly what arrives, including what it cannot parse). Its listener key simulacrumAdmin::gmcp is unique on purpose (A1/E26). onMessage hears every message even while paused, because characterInfo must not miss a login.

/dslGmcpSchema.ts
Purpose: DSL's seven GMCP packages as data (field types, optional fields, enum value sets), read from its live traffic via scripts/gmcp-corpus/. Refresh it by re-running those scripts; docs/game/gmcp-parity.md explains each choice. strictValues=false means the set is only what was SEEN (affect locations), so another value is only a note. knownDifferences are owner decisions (language words), shown as notes.

/gmcpParity.ts
Purpose: Pure parity check of captured messages against dslGmcpSchema. A finding repeats a value only for enum-like fields (never names or other free text). The affects list is checked element by element, so it is removed from the top-level field check to avoid a bogus extra-field note.

/gmcpView.ts
Purpose: Display limits for the GMCP tab (200 rows, 64 KB of detail) and the detail text. Kept out of the component file only because the lint rule wants component files to export components.

/characterInfo.ts
Purpose: The connected character's level and clan flag from login_data, memory only. The NAME is deliberately not kept (Personal data, no use for it). Level is not trust: wizhelp stays the authority on which commands the character can run.

/commandTable.generated.ts
Purpose: GENERATED by scripts/generate-simulacrum-admin-commands.mjs from merc-mud interp.c (privileged rows only). Never edit by hand; re-run the script after a game change. Hidden aliases (reboo, shutdow, sla, prefi, ":", invis) are listed so the panel can refuse to offer them.

/commandSyntax.ts
Purpose: Hand-written argument shapes for every generated command, read from each handler (the file named in each summary). `destructive` is the owner-approved confirmation set (S11, widened 2026-11-07 to every command that writes to a player or the server). Pair with the generated table: commandCatalog.test.ts fails on a missing entry or an orphan. A form with a `category` is listed on the Players tab and must start with the player target.

/commandSyntaxTypes.ts
Purpose: Types for commandSyntax.ts. Always-wide forms (restore all, purge with no target, copyover now) set `confirm`; value-dependent ones (transfer all, force players, ban *) are `bulk` rules on a field.

/commandCatalog.ts
Purpose: Joins the generated table and the syntax into COMMAND_CATALOG; buildCatalog is pure so drift can be tested with fixtures. findCatalogCommand never finds a hidden alias (E25).

/commandBuilder.ts
Purpose: The only place a command line is assembled: full command name, literal words, typed fields. Rejects control characters and over-255 lines naming the field (E4). Never abbreviates, so `reboo`/`shutdow` cannot be sent.

/confirmPolicy.ts
Purpose: Whether a send asks first, from the data in commandSyntax (destructive, confirm, bulk, safe) plus an inner-command check for `at`/`force`, which also catches abbreviations (the game runs the first row a word prefixes). Adding a command to the data needs no change here.

/verdict.ts
Purpose: Judges a reply from the game's own words (ADMIN-03): `Huh?` anywhere refuses; otherwise the first line that is a refusal or a success decides; else unknown. REFUSAL_PATTERNS are the handlers' own messages, anchored at line start so a room description is not read as a refusal; the refusal check runs before success on every line.

/replyCollector.ts
Purpose: Collects game:remote-server:raw text after a send. Joins chunks BEFORE stripping escapes (a split escape sequence), ends 600 ms after the last chunk or 4 s after the start, one collection at a time. Listener key `simulacrumAdmin::reply` (E26).

/sender.ts
Purpose: The ONLY dispatcher of shatteredarchive:send-command in the feature (S6). Connection check, build, confirmation callback, serialised sends (E24), verdict, activity entry, and the wizhelp list. Records nothing when the connection ended while waiting (E2).

/activityLog.ts
Purpose: Last 200 sends with verdict and reply, memory only; the loader clears it on disconnect.

/senderToSocket.test.ts
Purpose: Proves the built line reaches the websocket as a `data` message through the REAL useGameConnection hook (E5), with a fake socket playing the game.

/outcomeText.ts
Purpose: The one place a run outcome becomes the words shown (Done / Refused by the game (...) / unknown / not sent). Shared by every tab that runs commands.

/worldConfig.ts
Purpose: The base address of the world-data vhost and the owner's storage override. The override is accepted only as a bare origin on localhost, a private address or *.shatteredarchive.dev (LOCAL-05 rule, shared with the host additions via connectionGate), so a stored value cannot send requests to a public server.

/worldApi.ts
Purpose: The only two calls to the vhost (/api/map, /api/map/<file>). Failures are values (offline / error / aborted), never throws (E8). Hand-written validators: a wrong type rejects the whole answer. The file name is checked against the area store's pattern BEFORE it is put in a URL. Strips {x colour codes from names; keeps only vnum and name of each room.

/worldFilter.ts
Purpose: Pure filtering of areas (name, file, vnum in range, range overlap) and rooms (vnum exact/prefix, range, name). Input order is kept. Has a time-bound test for 3,200 rooms.

/useWorldIndex.ts
Purpose: Lazy area list, per-area rooms on demand, session cache, retry, refresh. Every request has an AbortSignal; unmount aborts them and an aborted result never writes state back.

/tabs.ts
Purpose: (updated) the six tab ids and labels only; every tab has a real panel now, so there are no placeholders.
